// Branch coverage for ssz: the package's own tests, and nothing else.
//
//   deno task coverage:ssz
//   deno task coverage:ssz --verbose
//
// **The first of the eighteen packages `issues/system/0205` records as having no coverage driver at
// all.** That issue's open half is not "should these numbers be floors" — every driver that exists is
// one now — but whether the eighteen unmeasured packages should have drivers, which is 82,762 source
// lines against 36,918 measured. A decision that has sat for three days wants an input rather than an
// argument: this is one package done, to find out what it costs and what it turns up.
//
// `ssz` was picked because it is representative rather than easy — 799 lines, 26 tests, twenty of them
// against Ethereum's own roots — and because of what a gap here would mean. A wrong Merkle root is not
// a crash: it is a proof that verifies against the wrong state, silently.
//
// There is no probe and no hand-written corpus. Every one of the 26 tests is called directly, which is
// what `issues/system/0221` made possible — twenty take `(Core, Cli)` because they read the vendored
// fixtures and ask a host-side oracle, and before that a driver could call none of them.
//
// None of them expects a trap, so there is no `trapCase` sweep.

import { Core, Cli } from "std/platform.wac";
import { itoa } from "../../fmt/src/itoa.wac";
